cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use diff-bwm-1, please cite it as below. If you use eval 4, please also
  cite AA-Briefcase-Lite (listed under references).
type: software
title: "diff-bwm-1: a six-eval benchmark for LLM planning agents grounded in numerical models"
abstract: >-
  diff-bwm-1 is a six-eval suite that tests whether an LLM planning agent that can
  run a numerical model of its domain behaves more like a programmer with code:
  internally consistent, and able to test a draft before shipping it. The package
  contains the evals, their scorers (a bit-for-bit "paper" ruleset and a corrected
  "v1" ruleset) and a harness that runs agents in isolated sandboxes.
authors:
  - name: Differential AI Lab
  - family-names: Hamilton
    given-names: Gabe
version: 1.0.0
# date-released: TODO(owner): set to the release date (YYYY-MM-DD) when the 1.0.0 tag is published.
# repository-code: TODO(owner): set once the public repository exists.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - LLM agents
  - planning
  - numerical models
  - calibration
  - overclaiming
references:
